    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d422">

                <pb facs="0400" n="390" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg390"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2531/187: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Philip</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-01T12:00:00-04:00">July 1, 1937—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        12:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>31. Department’s 26, June 30, 8 [<hi rendition="#italic">5</hi>] p.m.<anchor
                        n="21" xml:id="d422-f1"/> Although the Minister of Foreign Affairs has
                    assured me in reply to my suggestions that the Foreign Office would endeavor to
                    prepare a reply to the Embassy’s memorandum of the 9th instant [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">ultimo</hi>], I doubt if anything of much interest can
                    be expected.</p>
                <p>I have been informed confidentially that it has been decided here to make every
                    effort to arrive at an understanding satisfactory to the United States but the
                    present attitude seems to indicate the intention to await the outcome of the
                    exploratory conversation by Señor García with the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d422-f1" n="21" xml:id="d422-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram read as follows: “Please telegraph what, if any, reaction the
                    Foreign Office has shown with respect to the memorandum.” (611.2531/187a)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
